## 4. The δ Function

### 4.1 The Rule

The δ function is piecewise in (support, n₁, |n₂ − n₁|):

$$\delta(n_1, |n_2 - n_1|, \text{support}) = \begin{cases} +33 & n_1 = 0,\ \text{supp} = 64 \\ +6 & n_1 = 4,\ \text{supp} = 64 \\ 3(2 - n_1) & n_1 \in \{1, 3\},\ \text{supp} = 48 \\ 0 & n_1 \in \{5, 7\},\ |n_2 - n_1| = 2,\ \text{supp} = 48 \\ +0.5 & n_1 \in \{5, 7\},\ |n_2 - n_1| = 4,\ \text{supp} = 48 \\ 0 & n_1 \in \{2, 6\},\ \text{supp} = 32,\ n_1 \neq n_2 \\ +0.5 & n_1 = n_2 = 6,\ \text{supp} = 32 \end{cases}$$

### 4.2 The Branches

| Branch | Condition | δ | Framework expression |
|:-------|:----------|:--|:---------------------|
| 1 | n₁ = 0, supp = 64 | +33 | 2d² + 1 |
| 2 | n₁ = 4, supp = 64 | +6 | d + 2 |
| 3 | n₁ = 1, supp = 48 | +3 | d − 1 |
| 4 | n₁ = 3, supp = 48 | −3 | −(d − 1) |
| 5 | n₁ ∈ {5, 7}, \|n₂ − n₁\| = 2, supp = 48 | 0 | 0 |
| 6 | n₁ ∈ {5, 7}, \|n₂ − n₁\| = 4, supp = 48 | +0.5 | 2/d |
| 7 | n₁ ≠ n₂, supp = 32 | 0 | 0 |
| 8 | n₁ = n₂ = 6, supp = 32 | +0.5 | 2/d |

### 4.3 The Linear Rule for n₁ ∈ {1, 2, 3}

For n₁ ∈ {1, 2, 3}, the δ values follow a single formula:

$$\delta = (d - 1)(2 - n_1) = 3(2 - n_1)$$

| n₁ | δ | Particles |
|:---|:--|:----------|
| 1 | +3 | u, d |
| 2 | 0 | W, Z |
| 3 | −3 | s, μ |

This is a derived formula using d − 1 = 3.

### 4.4 The Special Cases

The remaining 8 modes have δ values not covered by the linear rule:

