## 10. Open Questions

1. **Why |n₂ − n₁|?** The rule uses the distance from the diagonal. The physical meaning of this distance is not derived. It may be related to the mode's position relative to the λ = 4 level set.

2. **Why n₁ = 6 for the support-32 special case?** The mode t at (6, 6) is the only support-32 mode with δ = +0.5. The reason n₁ = 6 is singled out is not derived.

3. **The 10% mass formula residual.** The mesh-native mass formula m = v_EW · 2^(−N/4·π/d) reproduces the masses at RMS 0.051 dex. The residual is not structural — it is the difference between the derived N/4 values and the observed masses. Whether the formula is exact or approximate is open.

4. **Flavor mixing.** The CKM and PMNS matrices are not addressed by this paper. They remain open.

5. **The 8×8 torus uniqueness for all lattices.** The 8×8 Torus paper tested a set of 64-site lattices. A full proof that 8×8 is the unique 64-site lattice with 14-fold degeneracy at a self-paired eigenvalue is not given.

